WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know our first guest
tonight from his work

00:00:01.468 --> 00:00:03.870
on "Miami Vice," "Nash Bridges,"
"Watchmen," and "Knives Out.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
He stars in the comedy serie
"Kenan,"

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:08.541
which airs Tuesday nights
at 8:30 right here at NBC.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Don Johnson.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:11.678 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you, Don?

00:00:11.678 --> 00:00:13.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm terrific, Seth.
How you doing?

00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:15.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm doing fantastic.
You know, Kenan's an old frien

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:17.684
of mine, and I've been
a long-time fan of yours,

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:20.787
so I was delighted to see
you were working together.

00:00:20.787 --> 00:00:23.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
How did you end up
in this project?

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:26.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Um...
Well, I was --

00:00:26.126 --> 00:00:28.528 size:81% position:41%
They plucked me out of
the unemployment line.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:33.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
and it was a good choice.

00:00:33.233 --> 00:00:39.773 size:84% position:42%
But -- No, I, you know,
I got a -- I got a --

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.674 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think it probably
all started --

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:43.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lorne and I have been friend
for a long time.

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:47.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
And about a year ago or so -
can't remember.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:51.851 line:92%
COVID has made my brain mush

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:54.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lorne asked me to do
a table read with Michael Cera

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:58.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I did, and then,
I never heard from him again

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:01.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I said, "Well,
that must have been a bust."

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.195 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:03.797 line:92%
But then, meanwhile, this --

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:05.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
He called me,
and he sent me this.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:06.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
He said, "Here,
take a look at this,

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:07.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
see what you think,
blah, blah, blah."

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:10.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
And here I am.
-Now we had Kenan on,

00:01:10.537 --> 00:01:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
who said it is both a deligh
to work with you,

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's also a delight
to hear stories

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:18.144 line:92%
about your work in the '80s.

00:01:18.144 --> 00:01:20.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
It did strike me
that maybe the "Miami Vice" se

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.750 align:start size:94% position:6%
was a little wilder
than the "Kenan" set.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:26.286 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh...
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.286 --> 00:01:29.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
It's all a little bit hazy

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.590 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.590 --> 00:01:31.958 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I think -- yeah.

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you know,
given that we pretty much

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:38.031 align:start size:94% position:6%
owned the city of Miami,
and --

00:01:38.031 --> 00:01:41.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we had a party sequenc
in every episode,

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:46.005 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was single,
and, you know,

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.174 line:92%
it was kind of like, um...

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:51.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
it was kind of, like, joyful

00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:53.913 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:57.117
-I'm very -- I'm very happ
you don't look back on it

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
with any regrets.
It just seems lovely.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:03.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't remember
one bad moment.

00:02:03.323 --> 00:02:04.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not one.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.759
-I can tell you, you know,
of course, the other thing

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:10.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
you guys did is you develope
a style, you know,

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
that maybe
was accurate to Miami,

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
but the rest of us didn't know
anything about it.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:15.535 line:92%
And this is a true story.

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.137 size:75% position:38%
I remember going off
to a school dance.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.439
You know, and I was probably 11,
12 years old.

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:21.875
And my Dad said,
"You should roll up your sleeves

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:24.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
of your blazer,
'Miami Vice'-style."

00:02:24.344 --> 00:02:28.414 align:start size:94% position:6%
Even as a kid I thought,
"I think you're wrong, Dad."

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.817 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:34.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He -- He was wrong.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:36.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
There were -- There were
a lot of fools

00:02:36.356 --> 00:02:37.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
that were trying
to pull that off,

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:38.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know,
let's face it.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:42.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, it's a --
it's a -- it's a thing.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:44.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
I think it helps --

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:47.567
it helps a lot to look lik
Don Johnson when you want

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
to pull off that look.
-Yeah.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:52.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I say that as a compliment.
-I thank you very much.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:54.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was joking.
You know, it's very flattering

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:59.045
that something that I did that
was out of practical reasons -

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know if you're
aware of this,

00:03:00.847 --> 00:03:04.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it's hotter than...
uh, in Miami.

00:03:04.117 --> 00:03:08.655 size:78% position:39%
And so I just started
taking off clothes.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:14.227
The socks, the belt,
that T-shirt was just the front.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:14.794 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.794 --> 00:03:17.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
The unstructured jackets
and the linen,

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:21.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
the linen clothes,
and even then, I said,

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.503 line:92%
"Hey, I'm still pretty damn hot.

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:26.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay!
These sleeves are going up."

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.473 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Well, it worked out.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess sometimes, yeah,
that's the mother of invention

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:34.247 size:84% position:42%
I want to ask, as well,
you know, you guys were

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:35.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
doing a show
obviously on location.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:39.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did that give you a good dea
more amount of freedom?

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:42.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you didn't have
the sort of NBC execs around

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:45.024
in the way they would
if you were in L.A. or New York?

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:49.128
-You know -- [ Laughs ] --
it was kind of -- it was -

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:52.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
it was kind of being maroone
a little bit.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:55.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because, you know,
we were up very early.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:57.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
And everybody in Californi
sleeps until --

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.739 size:84% position:42%
they don't even come in
until 10:00 or 11:00.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.908
And so by the time
they would come into the office,

00:04:01.908 --> 00:04:03.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
we already had a half a day'
work shot,

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:07.113
and they would be sending us
pages and changes and we'd go,

00:04:07.113 --> 00:04:08.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No, no, no,
you don't understand.

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:11.918 align:start size:94% position:6%
That boat is already gone.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:14.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they'd get --
I mean, we'd make stuff up

00:04:14.254 --> 00:04:16.556
you know, and just say,
"Oh, this is a good idea.

00:04:16.556 --> 00:04:18.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's do this."
'Cause we all came out of

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.460 line:92%
independent films and stuff.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:25.798
I mean, I'm not sure that we
even knew what a permit was.

00:04:25.798 --> 00:04:28.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just would say,
"Oh. Well, let's crash the car

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.335 align:start size:94% position:6%
here in the middle
of this intersection.

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
Watch out!
There's a couple people there.

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
We should probably
get rid of them."

00:04:32.138 --> 00:04:35.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah.
We were just kind of wild me

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:38.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
down there, going, you know --
making a crazy show.

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:40.413
-Well, it's so interesting
you say that, because, you know,

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:43.082
I feel like people might
forget now that it was --

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
it did feel
so much more cinematic

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:46.953
than what anybody was used t
on television at the time,

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:49.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so it made sense that
you guys all came from film,

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:52.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it certainly
showed up in the product.

00:04:52.425 --> 00:04:54.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it did.
You know, there was --

00:04:54.727 --> 00:04:58.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were all, like --
It was like --

00:04:58.398 --> 00:04:59.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
We were --
We all knew each other.

00:04:59.899 --> 00:05:03.469 size:88% position:44%
It was all kind of like,
you know, we knew that

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:07.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
what we were bringing
was better than what was there

00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:09.175 line:92%
And for us it wasn't really --

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:11.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, we didn't think
about it in terms of,

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, gosh,
we're starting something new."

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:16.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
We just started something
saying, "Well, if we're gonn

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:17.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
do this,
we're gonna do something

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:20.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's got some quality,
is a little more interesting

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
the music is better,
and the colors,

00:05:22.255 --> 00:05:26.326
it'll actually have a film -
a film color palette, you know

00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:28.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
where we won't use
certain colors.

00:05:28.561 --> 00:05:32.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like you never saw red
in "Miami Vice."

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:35.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, well, occasionally,
I saw red,

00:05:35.401 --> 00:05:37.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it was
for different reasons.

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:38.071 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:40.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, now, you know,
that was a long-running show

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:44.577
and then you did "Nash Bridges,"
which I, of course, remember

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:45.578 line:92%
you did with Cheech Marin

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:46.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you guys
had incredible chemistry.

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:49.482
I had no idea, and maybe thi
was better known at the time

00:05:49.482 --> 00:05:52.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Hunter S. Thompson
was sort of

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:54.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
behind the creation
of this show with you.

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:57.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, well, Hunter
was my neighbor in Aspen.

00:05:57.623 --> 00:06:00.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, gratefully,
I was just out of mortar range

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:01.427 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:04.530
-I was gonna say, he does no
sound like a great neighbor.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:07.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He -- Well, actually,
he was a fabulous neighbor

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:08.468 line:92%
Whenever I was out of town -

00:06:08.468 --> 00:06:12.305 align:start size:94% position:6%
You wouldn't know this
about Hunter, but he was -

00:06:12.305 --> 00:06:13.106 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
he loved animals.

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:15.274 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if I had a sick animal
he would --

00:06:15.274 --> 00:06:16.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was out of town --
he would come over

00:06:16.843 --> 00:06:21.147 size:81% position:41%
and sleep in the stall
with my animal, or in,

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:22.081 line:92%
you know, wherever they were

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:25.918
And, you know, he'd bring a fe
animals of his own for company

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:29.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
And -- But, no,
he was a fabulous friend.

00:06:29.522 --> 00:06:33.025
We were very, very close friends
for many, many years.

00:06:33.025 --> 00:06:36.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
And one time we were sitting
around over at his house,

00:06:36.496 --> 00:06:41.000
and probably some illegal
substances were around,

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:44.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we -- I said,
"Listen, I have this --"

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:47.140
Oh, he was complaining about
how he didn't have any money

00:06:47.140 --> 00:06:51.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "Well, look,
I got this commitment on CBS."

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:52.879 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You know, 22 episodes.

00:06:52.879 --> 00:06:54.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "Let's just
come up with something."

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:56.482 line:92%
We did come up with something.

00:06:56.482 --> 00:07:00.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was terrible.
But -- But he was there.

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:03.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was in the room.
So -- So, he got --

00:07:03.156 --> 00:07:05.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
He got to get a royalty.
And we --

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:08.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
I took the germ of the ide
that Hunter and I did,

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:10.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we turned it
into "Nash Bridges."

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.098 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Well, that's fantastic.

00:07:12.098 --> 00:07:14.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
What a fascinating neighbo
to have.

00:07:14.167 --> 00:07:14.901 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I have more to ask you.

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:18.504
We'll be right back with mor
from Don Johnson after this.

